    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with significant firepower at the top of the order, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) and **Yordan Alvarez** (74.28). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** earns the day's highest efficiency rating due to an ideal combination of lead-off positioning and a favorable matchup against Chandler, despite minor concerns regarding wind conditions. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in core play; while facing a mid-tier xERA in Peralta, his elite xwOBA of 0.443 provides an unmatched floor even in less-than-perfect park conditions. **Trea Turner** (73.97) and **Colt Keith** (69.64) round out our premier offensive threats, both benefiting from soft matchups against high-xERA starters and prime lineup slots that maximize their opportunities for runs and stolen base contributions, with the latter specifically bolstered by the high-SB environment expected against Hughes.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved the final utility spot, where **Kazuma Okamoto** (58.84) ultimately held off **Chase Meidroth** (49.89) to secure the start. While **Chase Meidroth** maintains a solid projection, he was downgraded by a negative park factor and a lower lineup placement, whereas **Kazuma Okamoto** receives a distinct platoon advantage against the lefty Rogers. We continue to monitor **Carson Benge** (43.39), who faces a tough assignment against the low-xERA Schlittler; while he remains in the lineup, his upside is constrained by the opposing arm\u2019s ability to stifle production. We are exercising caution with **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (41.39) and **Hector Rodriguez** (41.95), both of whom stayed on the bench due to significant platoon disadvantages or unfavorable order positioning. As we navigate the final stretch, we remain vigilant regarding the wind in the **Pedro Ramirez** matchup, which tempers his otherwise favorable SP skill rating.",
